<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-antirrhinum-majus-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Antirrhinum majus Turing ocellus wavelength at 259 µm (Holocene, 0 Ma) — Code-to-model traceability: 86/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The module docstring states the PDE, the trace, the determinant, and the distinction between argmax σ(k) and the Δ-minimizer. trace_det, sigma_of_k2, k_c_and_sigma, and grow_ocellus follow those lines. The Lean file names the same integers." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-antirrhinum-majus-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-antirrhinum-majus-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.6e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-antirrhinum-majus-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Antirrhinum majus Turing ocellus wavelength at 259 µm (Holocene, 0 Ma) — Model fidelity to source: 86/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The script integrates the stated Jacobian, the dispersion σ² − tr(k)σ + Δ(k) = 0, cubic saturation, and the equal-diffusion ablation. k_c is argmax σ(k), which is the selected wavelength off onset; the shortcut k² = h/(2 D_u D_v) is documented as a different quantity. Ten Lean theorems with zero sorry encode the integer trace, determinant, Turing margin, and the ablation. Deduction: the rates are reconstructed for this 259 µm slot, not fitted in a snapdragon paper, and the radial PSD that reads k back is biased (R1)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "models/2026-delphi10000-antirrhinum-majus-turing-wavelength-s0.py L197–L243: integer-pixel radial binning is the biased readback <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc/models/2026-delphi10000-antirrhinum-majus-turing-wavelength-s0.py#L197-L243>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-antirrhinum-majus-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-antirrhinum-majus-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.6e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-antirrhinum-majus-turing-wavelength-s0-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Antirrhinum majus Turing ocellus wavelength at 259 µm (Holocene, 0 Ma) — Morphometric validation: 84/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The gallery bar is detected as a 111 px white run and read as 100 µm. Four radial peaks give pitch 77.8 µm (CV of the gaps), foreground fraction, circularity, and structure-tensor coherency. Those values are not set equal to the model wavelength, so the comparison is not self-referential. KS of ring-gap samples is 1.0. Pearson r and RMSE are on the diffusivity sweep. Deduction: at unit scale the PSD peak reports λ ≈ 279 µm against λ_c = 259 µm (about 7% low in k). That bias is R1, not a hidden residual." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-antirrhinum-majus-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-analytical-critical-wavelength-lambda-c>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-antirrhinum-majus-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-diffusivity-scale-sweep-pearson-r-of-measured-vs-analytical-k-c>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-antirrhinum-majus-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-diffusivity-scale-sweep-rmse-of-wavenumber>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-antirrhinum-majus-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-domain-growth-mode-count-pearson-r>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-antirrhinum-majus-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-equal-diffusion-ablation-sigma-max>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-antirrhinum-majus-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-specimen-image-foreground-fraction>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-antirrhinum-majus-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-specimen-image-structure-tensor-coherency>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-antirrhinum-majus-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-specimen-ocellus-ring-spacing>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-antirrhinum-majus-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-successor-petal-mode-count-at-10-mm>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-antirrhinum-majus-turing-wavelength-s0-morphometric-validation-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-antirrhinum-majus-turing-wavelength-s0-morphometric-validation-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-antirrhinum-majus-turing-wavelength-s0-morphometric-validation-3> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.4e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-antirrhinum-majus-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Antirrhinum majus Turing ocellus wavelength at 259 µm (Holocene, 0 Ma) — MorphoEval overall 85.3/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Two-species activator-inhibitor system on a periodic petal-epidermis patch. Rates f_u, f_v, g_u, g_v = 1.25, -1.50, 2.00, -1.75 per hour; D_u, D_v = 640, 4341 µm²/h. Trace -0.50, determinant 0.8125, Turing margin positive, equal-diffusion control σ_max = -0.25 h⁻¹. k_c = argmax σ(k) gives λ_c = 259.13 µm at 0 Ma (assigned 259.2 µm). A joint diffusivity sweep (×0.35 to ×4) recovers k with Pearson r = 0.9992 and RMSE 0.00114 µm⁻¹. The gallery field's 100 µm bar (111 px) measures a ring pitch of 77.8 µm; KS against the simulated ring gaps is 1.0 because the two pitches do not overlap. GIF is 800×600, 12 frames. Computer-vision similarity of the last frame to the gallery field is 83.6. Overall 85.3. The radial PSD still reads k about 7% low at unit scale (remediation R1). Overall 85.3/100 (faithfulness 84.1, reproducibility 88.1); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 86, Morphological realism / specimen match 80, Parameter expressivity 91, Morphometric validation 84, Source and data traceability 90, Code-to-model traceability 86, Reproducibility package 88. Output judged: docs/media/antirrhinum_majus_turing_wavelength_s0_growth.gif: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-antirrhinum-majus-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc, image/gif, 3276935 B, 800×600 px, 12 frames, artifact_sha256 7ec4b0240db6d0c7bc707e1b06094421d59e6b3f85858e4a8f3daf5ebe4792bd (sha256 7ec4b0240db6d0c7bc707e1b06094421d59e6b3f85858e4a8f3daf5ebe4792bd), spec_fingerprint 9aa96d9174bbc264f2f19508483526998fd8a90a8bb5b00ee7c2a039134c8ca4. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 9aa96d9174bbc264f2f19508483526998fd8a90a8bb5b00ee7c2a039134c8ca4; artifact_sha256: 7ec4b0240db6d0c7bc707e1b06094421d59e6b3f85858e4a8f3daf5ebe4792bd; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/antirrhinum_majus_turing_wavelength_s0/antirrhinum_majus_sete_cc-by-sa.jpg=4d2cd99ca49de264..., datasets/antirrhinum_majus_turing_wavelength_s0/antirrhinum_majus_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=0918abca4751ad6b..., datasets/antirrhinum_majus_turing_wavelength_s0/antirrhinum_majus_turing_wavelength_s0_specimen.jpg=f3e9bf78a4453bc1...}. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Shang et al. 2010: Venosa MYB places anthocyanin over veins. | Noda et al. 1994: MIXTA conical epidermal cells intensify petal colour. | Turing 1952: diffusion-driven instability and a critical wavenumber.; reconstructed_in_script: Integer diffusivities D_u=640, D_v=4341 chosen so argmax σ(k) is 259.13 µm. | Split-step cubic saturation and the rendered radial ocellus.; transfer_boundary: Vein-locked Venosa pigment is not shown here to be a Turing instability. | The gallery ring pitch (77.8 µm) is a property of that asset, not a published histological wavelength.; does_not_claim: That Antirrhinum uses these kinetic constants in vivo. | That 77.8 µm and 259.13 µm are the same measurement.." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: {'id': 'R1', 'item': 'Radial PSD uses integer pixel bins and reads k about 7% low at unit diffusivity (measured λ ≈ 279 µm vs λ_c 259.13 µm). Re-bin in physical wavenumber and re-measure Pearson r and RMSE.'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R2', 'item': 'Single assessor. A second provider has not scored this script.'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R3', 'item': 'Annotate the kink in σ(k) at the edge of the unstable band so it is not mistaken for a numerical glitch.'}" ;
    pk:hasScore 8.53e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-antirrhinum-majus-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Antirrhinum majus Turing ocellus wavelength at 259 µm (Holocene, 0 Ma) — Parameter expressivity: 91/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Scaling D_u and D_v together from ×0.35 to ×4 moves λ_c from 153 µm to 518 µm. Measured Fourier peaks track analytical k_c with Pearson r = 0.9992 and RMSE 0.00114 µm⁻¹. The equal-diffusion ablation is outside that sweep and stays stable, so the wavelength control is the diffusivity scale, not a sign error." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-parameter-expressivity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/parameter-expressivity" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-antirrhinum-majus-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-antirrhinum-majus-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 9.1e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

